mainmenu "PWM cache loopback sample"

config SAMPLE_PAD_SIZE
	int "Size of the pad placed before the driver's sequence buffer [bytes]"
	default 28
	help
	  The pad shifts the pwm_nrfx sequence buffer (4 x uint16_t) inside the PWM DMA region.
	  With the 32-byte cache line and the pad of 28 bytes the buffer starts at offset 28 of
	  a line: channels 0-1 end up in one line and channels 2-3 in the next one.
	  Must be a multiple of 4. If the driver's buffer is not at the end of the pad (check
	  zephyr.map), the sample reports it and exits.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
